#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:38
msgid "Alt text describes each image's purpose"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:38
msgid "Open the Media Library and read the alt text of your key images. It should say what the image shows or does in context, not just repeat the file name. Purely decorative images should have empty alt text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:39
msgid "Videos have accurate captions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:39
msgid "Play each video with captions on. Captions should match the speech and include important sounds. Auto-generated captions usually need correcting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:40
msgid "Videos describe important visual information"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:40
msgid "If a video shows information only visually (on-screen text, actions), it needs narration or an audio-described version."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:41
msgid "Reading order makes sense"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:41
msgid "Turn off page styles (or use reader view) and read the page top to bottom. Content should still appear in a logical order."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:42
msgid "Instructions don't rely on shape, color, size or position alone"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:42
msgid "Look for instructions like \"click the green button\" or \"see the box on the right\" and add a text label to them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:43
msgid "Color is not the only way information is shown"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:43
msgid "Links in body text, required form fields, errors and chart data should also use underlines, text, icons or patterns."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:44
msgid "Tooltips and pop-ups on hover can be dismissed and hovered"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:44
msgid "Content that appears on hover or focus must close with Escape, stay open while the pointer moves onto it, and not vanish on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:45
msgid "Everything works with a keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:45
msgid "Put the mouse away. Use Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Space and arrow keys to use menus, forms, sliders, tabs and pop-ups."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:46
msgid "Keyboard focus never gets stuck"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:46
msgid "While tabbing, make sure you can always move focus out of every component, including embedded videos, maps and chat widgets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:47
msgid "Focus moves in a logical order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:47
msgid "Tab through each page template. Focus should follow the visual order, and open dialogs should receive focus."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:48
msgid "Headings and labels are descriptive"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:48
msgid "Each heading should tell you what the section is about, and each form label should say what to enter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:49
msgid "Focused items aren't hidden behind sticky headers or banners"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:49
msgid "Tab through pages with a sticky header, cookie banner or chat button visible. The focused element must stay at least partly visible."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:50
msgid "Anything you drag can also be done without dragging"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:50
msgid "Sliders, sortable lists and maps need a click or tap alternative, such as buttons."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:51
msgid "Navigation is consistent across pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:51
msgid "Menus and repeated links should appear in the same order on every page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:52
msgid "Form errors are clearly described in text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:52
msgid "Submit each form with mistakes. Every error should be explained in text next to the field, not only with a red border."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:53
msgid "Form errors suggest how to fix them"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:53
msgid "Error messages should say what is expected, for example \"Enter a date as DD/MM/YYYY\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:54
msgid "Users don't have to re-enter the same information"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:54
msgid "In multi-step forms or checkout, information entered earlier should be filled in or selectable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:55
msgid "Login doesn't require solving a puzzle or memorizing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:55
msgid "Login and account forms should allow password managers and paste, and avoid puzzle CAPTCHAs without an alternative."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:56
msgid "Status messages are announced to screen readers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:56
msgid "Messages like \"Added to cart\" or \"Form sent\" should be announced without moving focus. Test with a screen reader."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:57
msgid "Data tables make sense when read aloud"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:57
msgid "Check each data table: column and row headings should be marked as header cells, and the table should have a caption or heading that says what it shows. Avoid tables for layout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:58
msgid "Text can be zoomed to 200%"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:58
msgid "Zoom your browser to 200% (Ctrl or Cmd and +). All text should get bigger, and nothing should be cut off or overlap."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:59
msgid "Pages work on a narrow screen without sideways scrolling"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:59
msgid "Set your browser window to about 320px wide, or zoom to 400%. Content should fit the width, with no need to scroll left and right (except maps, data tables and similar)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:60
msgid "Text still works with extra spacing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:60
msgid "Use a text spacing bookmarklet to increase line, letter and word spacing. No text should be cut off or overlap."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:61
msgid "Time limits can be turned off or extended"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:61
msgid "If anything times out (sessions, forms, quizzes), visitors must be warned and able to extend the time, unless the limit is essential."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:62
msgid "Moving content can be paused"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:62
msgid "Carousels, sliders, animations and auto-playing video that last more than five seconds need a pause or stop button."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:63
msgid "Nothing flashes more than three times a second"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:63
msgid "Check videos, animations and GIFs. Content should not flash more than three times in one second, as it can trigger seizures."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:64
msgid "Page titles describe each page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:64
msgid "Look at the browser tab for each template. Every page should have a unique title that says what it is, for example \"Contact us - Your Site\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:65
msgid "Link text makes sense"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:65
msgid "Read the links on a page. Each should say where it goes, on its own or with the sentence around it. Replace \"click here\" with descriptive text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:66
msgid "Text in another language is marked"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:66
msgid "If a page contains a passage in another language, mark it with that language (in the block editor, select the text and use the Language option where available, or add a lang attribute) so screen readers pronounce it correctly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:67
msgid "Nothing changes unexpectedly when you focus or select something"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:67
msgid "Tab through forms and change dropdowns and options. The page should not jump, submit or open new windows unless you press a button."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:68
msgid "Content uses plain language and explains abbreviations"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:68
msgid "Read key pages as a newcomer. Use short sentences and common words, and spell out abbreviations the first time they appear. (A recommended practice, not a WCAG AA requirement.)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:69
msgid "One page tested with a screen reader"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-checklist.php:69
msgid "Use NVDA (Windows, free) or VoiceOver (Mac/iPhone, built in) to navigate your home page and one form. Note anything confusing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-compare.php:30
msgid "One of the audits could not be found."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-dismiss.php:32
msgid "Not a real problem (false positive)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-dismiss.php:33
msgid "Already accessible in a way the scan can't see"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-dismiss.php:34
msgid "Known issue, accepted for now"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-dismiss.php:67
msgid "That issue could not be found."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-editor.php:60
msgid "Check this element against the WCAG requirement shown, then update it in the block settings or ask your theme or plugin developer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:29
msgid "A screen reader instruction (ARIA) is used incorrectly"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:30 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:71 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:77 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:83 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:89 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:95 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:132 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:138 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:156 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:162 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:168 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:198 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:204 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:210 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:217 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:223 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:265 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:271 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:277 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:289 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:313 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:333 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:339 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:351 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:365 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:401 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:413 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:425 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:449 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:467 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:473 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:479 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:491 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:503 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:509 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:515
msgid "Screen reader users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:31
msgid "ARIA attributes tell assistive technology what an element is and what state it is in. When they are wrong or incomplete, screen readers announce confusing or false information, which can be worse than having no ARIA at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:32
msgid "Check the element's role and aria-* attributes against the expected pattern. Often the simplest fix is to use a native HTML element (button, link, input) instead of ARIA. This usually comes from a theme or plugin, so you may need to contact its developer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:36
msgid "Accessibility problem"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:37
msgid "People using assistive technology"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:38
msgid "This element does not meet a WCAG requirement, which can make it hard or impossible for some visitors to perceive or use."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:39
msgid "Open \"How to fix this\" for detailed guidance on this rule, then update the element in your content, theme or plugin settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:52
msgid "Images are missing a text description"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:53
msgid "Blind and low-vision visitors using screen readers; also search engines"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:54
msgid "Screen readers read an image's alt text out loud. Without it, visitors hear only \"image\" or the file name, so they miss whatever the picture shows or does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:55
msgid "Add alt text that describes what the image shows or does, in a short sentence. If the image is purely decorative, give it empty alt text so screen readers skip it. In WordPress, set this in the Media Library or the image block's settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:58
msgid "Images in your posts are missing a text description"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:59 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:65
msgid "Blind and low-vision visitors using screen readers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:60
msgid "This image was found in post content without any alt attribute, so screen readers have nothing to announce."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:61
msgid "Edit the post, select the image and fill in \"Alternative text\" in the block settings. Use empty alt text only for decorative images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:64
msgid "Media Library images have no alt text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:66
msgid "Alt text set in the Media Library is used automatically wherever the image is inserted later. Leaving it empty means every future use starts without a description."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:67
msgid "Go to Media > Library, open the image and fill in \"Alternative Text\". Leave it empty only if the image is purely decorative."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:70
msgid "Graphics marked as images have no description"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:72
msgid "This element is announced as an image but has no text alternative, so its meaning is lost."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:73
msgid "Add an aria-label or aria-labelledby that describes the graphic, or remove role=\"img\" if it is decorative."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:76
msgid "SVG images have no description"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:78
msgid "Icons and illustrations drawn as SVG need a text alternative just like regular images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:79
msgid "Add a <title> inside the SVG or an aria-label on it. If the icon is decorative, add aria-hidden=\"true\" instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:82
msgid "Image buttons have no text alternative"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:84
msgid "A button made from an image needs alt text that says what the button does, or users won't know what will happen when they press it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:85
msgid "Add alt text describing the action, for example \"Search\" or \"Submit order\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:88
msgid "Clickable areas of an image map have no text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:90
msgid "Each clickable area works like a link and needs text saying where it goes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:91
msgid "Add alt text to every <area> element describing its destination."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:94
msgid "Embedded objects have no text alternative"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:96
msgid "Embedded content such as old plugins or documents needs a description so everyone knows what it contains."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:97
msgid "Add an aria-label or title to the <object>, or provide the content another way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:100
msgid "Text is hard to read against its background"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:101
msgid "People with low vision or color blindness, older visitors, anyone reading on a phone in sunlight"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:102
msgid "When text and background colors are too similar, the text fades out. WCAG asks for a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:103
msgid "Make the text darker or the background lighter (or the opposite on dark designs) until the ratio passes. You can usually change these colors in your theme's style settings or the block's color settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:106
msgid "Links in text can only be spotted by color"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:107
msgid "People with color blindness or low vision"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:108
msgid "If a link looks just like the surrounding text except for its color, some visitors can't tell it's a link."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:109
msgid "Underline links in body text, or give them enough contrast with the surrounding text plus a visible change on hover and focus."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:112
msgid "Links don't say where they go"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:113 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:119
msgid "Screen reader and voice control users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:114
msgid "This link has no readable text, often because it only contains an icon or an image without alt text. Screen readers announce it as just \"link\", and voice users can't say its name to click it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:115
msgid "Add visible link text, or alt text to the image inside the link, or an aria-label such as \"Read more about our services\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:118
msgid "Buttons have no name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:120
msgid "A button with only an icon, or nothing at all, is announced as just \"button\". Visitors can't tell what it does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:121
msgid "Give the button visible text, or an aria-label that describes its action, such as \"Open menu\" or \"Search\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:125
msgid "Form fields have no label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:126
msgid "Screen reader users, people with cognitive disabilities, everyone filling in forms"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:127
msgid "Without a label, screen readers can't say what a field is for. Placeholder text alone disappears as soon as you type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:128
msgid "Add a visible <label> connected to each field. Most form plugins have a \"label\" setting; make sure it isn't hidden or empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:131
msgid "Dropdown menus have no label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:133
msgid "Screen readers can't say what a dropdown is for when it has no label."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:134
msgid "Add a visible label connected to the dropdown."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:137
msgid "Form fields have more than one label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:139
msgid "Different screen readers pick different labels when a field has several, so some users hear the wrong one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:140
msgid "Keep one label per field and remove the extra ones."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:143
msgid "Form fields use an invalid autofill hint"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:144
msgid "People with motor or memory difficulties who rely on autofill"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:145
msgid "Correct autocomplete values let browsers fill in names, emails and addresses automatically. A wrong value breaks that help."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:146
msgid "Use a standard autocomplete value such as \"email\", \"name\" or \"postal-code\", or remove the attribute."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:149
msgid "The page doesn't say what language it is in"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:150
msgid "Screen reader users; translation tools"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:151
msgid "Screen readers use the page language to pick the right voice and pronunciation. Without it, text may be read with the wrong accent and become hard to understand."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:152
msgid "Make sure your theme prints the language on the <html> tag. In WordPress this comes from Settings > General > Site Language and the theme's language_attributes() call."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:155
msgid "The page language code is not valid"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:157
msgid "An unrecognized language code means screen readers can't choose the right pronunciation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:158
msgid "Use a valid code like \"en\", \"en-US\" or \"ur\". Check Settings > General > Site Language."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:161
msgid "A section uses an invalid language code"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:163
msgid "Parts of a page can be marked as another language, but the code must be valid for screen readers to switch voices."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:164
msgid "Correct the lang attribute on that element to a valid language code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:167
msgid "The page declares two different languages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:169
msgid "The lang and xml:lang attributes disagree, so assistive technology may pick the wrong one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:170
msgid "Make both attributes match, or remove xml:lang."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:173
msgid "The page has no title"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:174
msgid "Screen reader users, people with many tabs open, search engines"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:175
msgid "The page title is the first thing a screen reader announces and what appears in the browser tab. Without it, visitors can't tell pages apart."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:176
msgid "Make sure your theme supports \"title-tag\" and every page has a descriptive title."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:179
msgid "There is no way to skip straight to the main content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:180 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:295 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:345 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:377 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:407 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:455 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:485
msgid "Keyboard and screen reader users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:181
msgid "Without a \"Skip to content\" link or proper page landmarks, keyboard users must tab through the whole menu on every single page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:182
msgid "Add a \"Skip to content\" link as the first focusable item, and wrap the main content in a <main> element. Many themes include this option."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:185
msgid "Zooming is blocked on mobile"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:186
msgid "People with low vision on phones and tablets"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:187
msgid "The page stops visitors from pinch-zooming, so people who need larger text can't enlarge it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:188
msgid "Remove \"user-scalable=no\" and any \"maximum-scale\" below 2 from the viewport meta tag in your theme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:191
msgid "The page refreshes or redirects on a timer"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:192
msgid "Screen reader users, people who read slowly"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:193
msgid "Automatic refreshes can move people away before they finish reading and reset their place on the page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:194
msgid "Remove the timed refresh, or use a server redirect instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:197
msgid "Lists contain items that aren't list items"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:199
msgid "Screen readers announce how many items a list has and let users jump between them. Other elements placed directly inside the list break that structure."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:200
msgid "Make sure <ul> and <ol> contain only <li> elements directly. This often comes from a theme or menu plugin, so you may need to ask its developer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:203
msgid "List items are placed outside a list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:205
msgid "A list item outside a list isn't announced as part of a group, so the structure is lost."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:206
msgid "Wrap <li> elements in a <ul> or <ol>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:209
msgid "Definition lists are structured incorrectly"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:211
msgid "Terms and definitions must be paired correctly to be announced together."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:212
msgid "Make sure <dl> contains only <dt> and <dd> groups."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:216
msgid "Embedded content (iframes) has no title"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:218
msgid "Videos, maps and widgets embedded in frames need a title so visitors know what the embedded area contains before entering it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:219
msgid "Add a title attribute to the iframe, for example title=\"Map of our office location\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:222
msgid "Several embedded frames share the same title"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:224
msgid "Identical titles make it impossible to tell embedded areas apart."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:225
msgid "Give each iframe a unique, descriptive title."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:228
msgid "Interactive content inside a frame can't be reached by keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:229 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:253
msgid "Keyboard users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:230
msgid "The frame is removed from the tab order but contains things you can click, so keyboard users can't reach them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:231
msgid "Remove tabindex=\"-1\" from the iframe."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:234
msgid "Videos have no captions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:235
msgid "Deaf and hard-of-hearing visitors; anyone watching with the sound off"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:236
msgid "Without captions, everything said in the video is lost for people who can't hear it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:237
msgid "Add a captions track to the video (a .vtt file), or use a video host such as YouTube that supports edited captions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:240
msgid "Audio plays automatically"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:241
msgid "Screen reader users, people with attention or anxiety conditions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:242
msgid "Sound that starts on its own can drown out a screen reader, and visitors may not find how to stop it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:243
msgid "Turn off autoplay, or make sure it stops within 3 seconds and has a clear pause control."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:246
msgid "Clickable elements are placed inside other clickable elements"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:247 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:283
msgid "Screen reader and keyboard users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:248
msgid "A button inside a link (or similar) confuses assistive technology, and the inner control may never be announced or reachable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:249
msgid "Restructure the element so links and buttons are not nested inside each other."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:252
msgid "Scrollable areas can't be scrolled with a keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:254
msgid "Content in a scrolling box is out of reach if keyboard users can't move focus into the box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:255
msgid "Add tabindex=\"0\" and an accessible name to the scrollable area, or make sure it contains a focusable element."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:258
msgid "Buttons or links are too small to tap easily"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:259
msgid "People with tremors or limited dexterity, everyone on a phone"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:260
msgid "Tiny targets packed close together lead to mis-taps. WCAG 2.2 asks for at least 24 by 24 pixels, or enough space around smaller targets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:261
msgid "Increase the size or padding of the link or button, or add more space between neighbouring targets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:264
msgid "Table cells point to headers that don't exist"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:266
msgid "Screen readers announce each cell's headers. Broken references mean cells are read without context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:267
msgid "Make sure every id in a cell's headers attribute matches a header cell in the same table."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:270
msgid "Table headers don't describe any data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:272
msgid "Header cells that don't relate to any data cells make the table structure confusing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:273
msgid "Use header cells only for real row or column headings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:276
msgid "Elements referenced by labels share the same id"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:278
msgid "When two elements have the same id, labels and descriptions may point to the wrong one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:279
msgid "Give every element a unique id."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:282
msgid "Hidden elements can still receive keyboard focus"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:284
msgid "The element is hidden from screen readers but can still be tabbed to, so users land on something that is announced as nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:285
msgid "Remove aria-hidden, or make the focusable items inside it unfocusable (for example with the inert attribute)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:288
msgid "The whole page is hidden from screen readers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:290
msgid "aria-hidden on the page body makes the entire site invisible to assistive technology."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:291
msgid "Remove aria-hidden=\"true\" from the <body> element. This is often left behind by a pop-up or menu script."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:294
msgid "Server-side image maps are used"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:296
msgid "Server-side image maps only work with a mouse."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:297
msgid "Replace it with regular links or a client-side image map with alt text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:300
msgid "Blinking content is used"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:301
msgid "People with attention or vision conditions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:302
msgid "Blinking text is distracting and hard to read, and can't be paused."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:303
msgid "Remove the <blink> element."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:306
msgid "Scrolling text (marquee) is used"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:307
msgid "People with attention, reading or vision conditions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:308
msgid "Moving text is hard to read and can't be paused."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:309
msgid "Replace the <marquee> with static text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:312
msgid "Expandable sections have no name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:314
msgid "The toggle for an expandable section has no text, so visitors don't know what it opens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:315
msgid "Add text inside the <summary> element."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:320
msgid "Headings with no text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:321
msgid "Screen reader users, who often move around a page by its headings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:322
msgid "An empty heading is announced as just \"heading\", which is confusing and wastes time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:323
msgid "Add text to the heading, or remove it if it is only used for spacing. In the block editor, look for empty Heading blocks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:326
msgid "Heading levels are skipped"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:327
msgid "Screen reader users and anyone scanning the page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:328
msgid "Headings form an outline of the page. Jumping from a level 2 straight to a level 4 suggests content is missing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:329
msgid "Use heading levels in order (H2, then H3 inside it). Choose the level for its place in the outline, and change the size with styles instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:332
msgid "Table headers with no text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:334
msgid "Screen readers read the column or row header before each cell. An empty header leaves those cells without context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:335
msgid "Add a short label to every header cell, or make the cell a normal data cell if it is not a header."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:338
msgid "Image alt text repeats the text next to it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:340
msgid "When an image's alt text repeats the link or caption text beside it, screen readers say the same thing twice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:341
msgid "Leave the alt text empty if the nearby text already says it, or describe something the text doesn't."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:344
msgid "Keyboard order is forced with tabindex"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:346
msgid "A tabindex above 0 makes those elements jump to the front of the keyboard order, so focus moves around the page unpredictably."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:347
msgid "Remove tabindex values above 0 and arrange the content in a logical order instead. This often comes from a theme or plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:350
msgid "An element has a role that doesn't suit it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:352
msgid "A role tells screen readers what something is. A role that conflicts with the element, such as an image marked decorative that still has a description, sends mixed signals."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:353
msgid "Remove the role attribute, or use an element that matches what it does. For decorative images, use empty alt text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:356
msgid "Page has no main heading (H1)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:357
msgid "Screen reader users and search engines"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:358
msgid "The main heading tells visitors what the page is about, and many screen reader users jump to it first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:359
msgid "Give each page one H1 heading, usually the page title. Some themes hide it on the home page; check your theme settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:364
msgid "Links with only a symbol as text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:366
msgid "A link whose text is just a symbol such as \"»\" or \".\" is announced as that symbol, so people can't tell where it goes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:367
msgid "Add words that describe the destination, for example \"Next page\". If you keep the symbol, add visually hidden text or an aria-label."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:370
msgid "Link text like \"Click here\" or \"Read more\""
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:371
msgid "Screen reader users, who often list all links on a page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:372
msgid "Out of context, \"Read more\" or \"Click here\" doesn't say where a link goes. Screen reader users often browse a list of links on their own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:373
msgid "Make the link text describe the destination, for example \"Read more about our opening hours\". You can hide the extra words visually if needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:376
msgid "Links that don't go anywhere"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:378
msgid "A link with href=\"#\" or a javascript: address usually acts as a button. Screen readers announce it as a link, and it may not work with the Space key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:379
msgid "If it opens or controls something on the page, use a <button>. If it should go somewhere, give it a real address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:382
msgid "File links don't say the file type"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:383
msgid "Everyone, especially screen reader and mobile users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:384
msgid "People expect a link to open a web page. A PDF or Word file can be slow to download and hard to use on some devices."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:385
msgid "Add the file type (and ideally the size) to the link text, for example \"Annual report (PDF, 2 MB)\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:388
msgid "Audio or video files may need a transcript"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:389 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:521 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:527
msgid "People who are deaf or hard of hearing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:390
msgid "Audio and video content needs a text alternative so everyone can get the information."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:391
msgid "Provide a transcript next to the link, or captions for video."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:394
msgid "Links open a new tab without warning"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:395
msgid "Screen reader, keyboard and older users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:396
msgid "A new tab or window opening unexpectedly can be disorienting, and the Back button no longer works."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:397
msgid "Avoid opening new tabs where possible. If you must, add \"(opens in a new tab)\" to the link text or as visually hidden text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:400
msgid "Link title repeats the link text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:402
msgid "A title attribute that repeats the link text adds nothing and may be read twice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:403
msgid "Remove the title attribute, or use it only for extra information that is also available another way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:406
msgid "Two links side by side go to the same place"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:408
msgid "An image link and a text link next to each other that go to the same page mean two tab stops and the same link announced twice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:409
msgid "Wrap the image and the text in one link."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:412
msgid "Links with the same text go to different pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:414
msgid "When several links have identical text but different destinations, people can't tell them apart in a list of links."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:415
msgid "Make each link's text unique, for example by adding the item name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:418
msgid "Fields use placeholder text instead of a label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:419
msgid "People with memory or cognitive disabilities, and screen reader users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:420
msgid "Placeholder text disappears when someone starts typing, and it is often low contrast. People then forget what the field was for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:421
msgid "Add a visible label to the field. Keep the placeholder only for an example, if at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:424
msgid "Tables without header cells"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:426
msgid "Without header cells, screen readers can't tell people which column or row a value belongs to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:427
msgid "Mark the first row or column as headers (th). In the block editor, turn on \"Header section\" for the Table block. If the table is only for layout, add role=\"presentation\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:430
msgid "Very small text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:431
msgid "People with low vision and older visitors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:432
msgid "Text smaller than 12px is hard to read for many people, even if they can zoom."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:433
msgid "Use at least 14 to 16px for body text and at least 12px for small print."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:436
msgid "Long text is justified"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:437
msgid "People with dyslexia or low vision"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:438
msgid "Justified text stretches the gaps between words unevenly, creating \"rivers\" of white space that make reading harder."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:439
msgid "Align body text to the left (or right, for right-to-left languages)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:442
msgid "Long text in capital letters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:443
msgid "People with dyslexia or low vision, and screen reader users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:444
msgid "Text in capitals is harder to read in long passages, and some screen readers spell it out letter by letter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:445
msgid "Write the text in normal case. Use capitals only for short labels, preferably with CSS text-transform."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:448
msgid "Empty paragraphs used for spacing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:450
msgid "Empty paragraphs are sometimes announced as \"blank\", which is confusing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:451
msgid "Remove the empty paragraphs and use block spacing or a Spacer block instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:454
msgid "Access keys are used"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:456
msgid "Access keys can clash with shortcuts in browsers and screen readers, and users rarely know they exist."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:457
msgid "Remove the accesskey attribute."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:460
msgid "Animated images may need a pause option"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:461
msgid "People with attention disorders or vestibular conditions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:462
msgid "Moving images that play for more than five seconds can make it impossible to concentrate on the rest of the page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:463
msgid "Use a still image, or a video with a pause button, if the animation lasts more than five seconds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:466
msgid "Groups of form fields need a clear legend"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:468
msgid "A fieldset groups related fields, and its legend tells people what the group is about. Without a legend, the group has no name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:469
msgid "Add a <legend> with text as the first element inside the <fieldset>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:472
msgid "Related radio buttons and checkboxes aren't grouped"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:474
msgid "When related options aren't grouped, screen reader users hear each option without the question it answers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:475
msgid "Put the options in a <fieldset> with a <legend> that asks the question."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:478
msgid "Images marked decorative still have a title"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:480
msgid "An image with empty alt text is hidden from screen readers, but a title attribute suggests it has information. The two signals conflict."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:481
msgid "If the image is decorative, remove the title. If it has information, put it in the alt text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:484
msgid "Keyboard focus lands on something that isn't interactive"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:486
msgid "An element with tabindex=\"0\" receives keyboard focus, but if it isn't a button, link or control, people land on it and nothing happens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:487
msgid "Remove tabindex from non-interactive elements, or give the element a proper role and keyboard behavior."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:490
msgid "Table cells aren't linked to their headers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:492
msgid "In complex tables, screen readers rely on scope or headers attributes to say which headers belong to each cell."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:493
msgid "Add scope=\"col\" or scope=\"row\" to header cells. For complex tables, split them into simpler ones or use headers and id attributes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:496
msgid "Outdated HTML is used"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:497
msgid "Everyone using assistive technology"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:498
msgid "Old elements such as <center> or <font> are no longer part of HTML and may not be supported in the future."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:499
msgid "Replace them with modern HTML and CSS. This often comes from older content or a theme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:502
msgid "Alt text may not describe the image"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:504
msgid "The alt text looks like a file name or placeholder, so it may not tell people what the image shows."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:505
msgid "Write alt text that describes what the image shows or does in context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:508
msgid "Text may look like a heading without being one"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:510
msgid "Bold or large text styled as a heading isn't announced as a heading, so people can't jump to it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:511
msgid "If the text is a heading, use a real Heading block (H2, H3...)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:514
msgid "Content may be a list without list markup"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:516
msgid "Items written as lines of text (for example with dashes) aren't announced as a list, so people don't know how many items there are."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:517
msgid "Use a List block (bulleted or numbered) for lists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:520
msgid "Audio may need a transcript"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:522
msgid "Audio content needs a text transcript so everyone can get the information."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:523
msgid "Add a transcript below the audio player or link to one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:526
msgid "Video may need captions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:528
msgid "Videos with speech need captions that match what is said."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:529
msgid "Add a captions track to the video. Check auto-generated captions for accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:549 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:550 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:551 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:552 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:553
msgid "Some images are missing a text description"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:554
msgid "Some text has low color contrast"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:555
msgid "Some links don't describe where they go"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:556
msgid "Some buttons have no accessible name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:557
msgid "Some form fields have no label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:558 includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:559
msgid "Some lists are not structured correctly"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:560
msgid "Some buttons or links are small to tap"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:561
msgid "Some videos have no captions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:576
msgid "The CoreA11y score is our own quick progress indicator from 0 to 100, based only on the automated checks. It goes down with each problem found, weighted by severity, and averaged per page. It is not an official WCAG score or a compliance grade, and other tools score differently: a site can score well and still have issues automated tools can't detect."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:577
msgid "A widely recommended practice that makes pages easier to use, but isn't a strict WCAG requirement. Shown as minor and never counted in the score."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:578
msgid "Elements the automated checks could not judge with certainty, such as text over an image or gradient, where a person needs to look. They are listed so nothing is hidden, but they are not counted as issues."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:579
msgid "The number of individual elements with a problem. One missing alt text on five images counts as five issues."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:580
msgid "The number of different kinds of problems found. Fixing one kind (for example, in your theme) often clears many issues at once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:581
msgid "Pages successfully scanned out of the pages planned. Change which pages are scanned in Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:582
msgid "Critical: blocks some visitors completely, for example a button a screen reader can't identify. Fix these first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:583
msgid "Serious: causes major difficulty for some visitors, for example hard-to-read text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:584
msgid "Moderate: creates friction but visitors can usually work around it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:585
msgid "Minor: small annoyances that are still worth fixing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:586
msgid "Fixes that have one correct answer and can be applied safely and undone, like adding the page language. Turn them on under CoreA11y > Quick fixes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:587
msgid "Fixes that change how something looks or reads, like a text color. CoreA11y Pro suggests a fix and applies it once you approve."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:588
msgid "Fixes only you can make well, like writing a meaningful description of a photo or adding captions to a video."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:589
msgid "Issues found in the earlier audit that are no longer found in the later one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:590
msgid "Issues found in both audits."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-explain.php:591
msgid "Issues found in the later audit that were not in the earlier one, for example on a new page or after a theme change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:32
msgid "Add a \"Skip to content\" link"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:33
msgid "Adds a link that appears when keyboard users press Tab, letting them jump past the menu straight to the main content. It is skipped if your theme already has one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:38
msgid "Show a clear keyboard focus outline"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:39
msgid "Draws a high-contrast outline around links, buttons and fields when they are reached with the keyboard, even if your theme removed it. Mouse clicks are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:44
msgid "Add the page language"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:45
msgid "Tells screen readers which language your pages are in, using the language from Settings > General, so text is pronounced correctly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:50
msgid "Allow pinch-zoom on phones"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:51
msgid "Removes the setting some themes use to block zooming, so visitors who need bigger text can zoom in on mobile."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:56
msgid "Label search and comment fields"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:57
msgid "Gives WordPress search boxes and comment form fields a name screen readers can announce, when your theme leaves it out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:62
msgid "Add a missing page title"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:63
msgid "Gives every page a title (shown in the browser tab and read first by screen readers) when your theme does not output one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:68
msgid "Title embedded videos, maps and widgets"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:69
msgid "Adds a title such as \"YouTube video\" or \"Map\" to embedded frames that have none, so screen reader users know what they contain."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:74
msgid "Hide empty headings from screen readers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:75
msgid "Empty headings, often left by page builders, are hidden from screen readers so they aren't announced as blank headings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:80
msgid "Hide empty paragraphs from screen readers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:81
msgid "Empty paragraphs used for spacing are hidden from screen readers so they aren't announced as \"blank\". The spacing stays."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:86
msgid "Restore the natural keyboard order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:87
msgid "Removes forced keyboard order (tabindex above 0), so Tab moves through the page in the order it is read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:92
msgid "Remove clashing keyboard shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:93
msgid "Removes access keys, which can clash with screen reader and browser shortcuts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:98
msgid "Respect \"reduce motion\" settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:99
msgid "For visitors who ask their device for less motion, animations and smooth scrolling are switched off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-corea11y-fixes.php:539
msgid "Skip to content"
msgstr ""

